(KEY-21 — `Mount` and `Unmount`/`Umount` start the mount statements. Run
 unprivileged this records the refusal path (the error flag is set and the
 program continues); the success path needs root. All three spellings
 compile.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox KEY-21.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   mount refused
   unmount refused
   lazy umount refused
   still running
)
Create a directory called "/tmp/voxfuzz-key-21".
Mount "tmpfs" at "/tmp/voxfuzz-key-21" with type "tmpfs" with options "size=1m".
On error print "mount refused".
Unmount "/tmp/voxfuzz-key-21".
On error print "unmount refused".
Umount "/tmp/voxfuzz-key-21" lazily.
On error print "lazy umount refused".
Remove the directory called "/tmp/voxfuzz-key-21".
Print "still running".
